\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5u+v-6 \\\\ 2u+4v\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5u+v \\\\ 2u+4v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c = 1+2+0 = 3.\n$$" 13194139535926 false] [17592186171831 1145 "An affine transformation $\\mathbf T:\\mathbb R^2\\rightarrow\\mathbb R^2$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf x = A \\mathbf u + \\mathbf b,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x, \\mathbf u,$ and $\\mathbf b$ are column vectors in $\\mathbb R^2,$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/assets/514520062cf4564f58267774ba6b50027f9cd27dedfa392cb7038f94580b1e4a.png)\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5u+v-6 \\\\ 2u+4v\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5u+v \\\\ 2u+4v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c = 1+2+0 = 3.\n$$" 13194139535926 true] [17592186171832 1100 "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx = 3u-v + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{a}, \\qquad y = u + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{b}v + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{c}\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139535926 false] [17592186171832 1100 "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx = 3u-v + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{a}, \\qquad y = u + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{b}v + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{c}\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072116/assets/43bcde1806155410ba97b0b2e5807d4a0f9cee93ef04f2ccfb413552de74178b.png)" 13194139535926 true] [17592186172024 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374779 13194139535926 true] [17592186172024 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374786 13194139535926 true] [17592186172025 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374813 13194139535926 true] [17592186172026 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374799 13194139535926 true] [17592186172026 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374806 13194139535926 true] [17592186172227 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535926 true] [17592186172227 1100 "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=-u+av+b,\\,y=2u-5v+c\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139535926 true] [17592186172227 1100 "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$x =-u + av + b, y = 2u - 5v + c$\nis shown below. What is the value of $a + b + c$?\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139535926 false] [17592186172227 1145 "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWe can carry out the matrix operations using the matrix form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot \\overset{u}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}}+\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-u+4v \\\\ 2u-5v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-u+4v+2 \\\\ 2u-5v+1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding elements, we obtain\n\n$$\nx=-u+4v+2,\\,y=2u-5v+1\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=4+2+1=7.\n$$" 13194139535926 true] [17592186172228 1017 #edb/ref 17592186168571 13194139535926 false] [17592186172228 1017 #edb/ref 17592186374793 13194139535926 true] [17592186172228 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535926 true] [17592186172228 1100 "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n- ${T}_{1}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}v-7u+3 \\\\ 3v-u+1\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{2}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}uv+1 \\\\ u-2v\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{3}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}9u \\\\ u-v\\end{aligned}]$" 13194139535926 true] [17592186172228 1100 "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n1. $T_{1}: \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}v - 7u + 3 \\\\ 3v - u + 1\\end{bmatrix}$\n2. $T_{2}: \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}uv + 1 \\\\ u - 2v\\end{bmatrix}$\n3. $T_{3}: \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}9u \\\\ u - v\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139535926 false] [17592186172228 1145 "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{1}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}v-7u+3 \\\\ 3v-u+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-7u+v \\\\ -u+3v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is not affine since it contains the cross term $uv.$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{3}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}9u \\\\ u-v\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9u \\\\ u-v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn fact, the transformation ${T}_{3}$ is a linear transformation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only.\"" 13194139535926 true] [17592186172230 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535926 true] [17592186172230 1100 "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=5u+3,\\,y=7v-u\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}a & 0 \\\\ b & 7\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139535926 true] [17592186172230 1100 "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$x = 5u + 3, y = 7v - u$\nis shown below. What is the value of $a + b + c$?\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}a & 0 \\\\ b & 7\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}c \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139535926 false] [17592186172230 1145 "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5u+3 \\\\ 7v-u\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5u+3 \\\\ 7v-u\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5u \\\\ -u+7v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 7\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=5+(-1)+3=7.\n$$" 13194139535926 true] [17592186374779 1017 #edb/ref 17592186374780 13194139535926 true] [17592186374779 1089 "q-124237" 13194139535926 true] [17592186374779 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535926 true] [17592186374779 1100 "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n- ${T}_{1}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}v-6u+7 \\\\ 4u+3v-5\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{2}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}-7u-2v \\\\ 5u+v\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{3}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}2u+v \\\\ uv+1\\end{aligned}]$" 13194139535926 true] [17592186374779 1113 #uuid "ac6412d1-cb10-5766-a34f-06f77acc0dfb" 13194139535926 true] [17592186374779 1145 "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{1}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}v-6u+7 \\\\ 4u+3v-5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6u+v \\\\ 4u+3v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{2}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-7u-2v \\\\ 5u+v\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-7u-2v \\\\ 5u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-7 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn fact, the transformation ${T}_{2}$ is a linear transformation.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is not affine since it contains the cross term $uv.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{2}$ only.\"" 13194139535926 true] [17592186374780 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374781 13194139535926 true] [17592186374780 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374782 13194139535926 true] [17592186374780 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374783 13194139535926 true] [17592186374780 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374784 13194139535926 true] [17592186374780 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374785 13194139535926 true] [17592186374780 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535926 true] [17592186374780 1041 "selection" 13194139535926 true] [17592186374780 1104 #edb/ref 17592186374784 13194139535926 true] [17592186374780 1110 #uuid "dd2eb17b-7d2b-5a7d-84d3-216b6cdf99dc" 13194139535926 true] [17592186374781 1034 "${T}_{1}$ only" 13194139535926 true] [17592186374781 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535926 true] [17592186374781 1111 #uuid "4db05b93-9101-50eb-867f-1be169ca5a25" 13194139535926 true] [17592186374782 1034 "${T}_{2}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only" 13194139535926 true] [17592186374782 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535926 true] [17592186374782 1111 #uuid "d2df3a64-9ca4-58c0-a5ed-0c2937f9db1d" 13194139535926 t